            <ArticleTitle>Mania associated with codeine and paracetamol.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>586-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">We describe a patient in whom a manic episode was precipitated by use of panadeine forte, a preparation containing codeine and paracetamol.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CLINICAL PICTURE" NlmCategory="METHODS">The patient developed a discrete manic psychotic episode.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="TREATMENT" NlmCategory="METHODS">The treatment consisted of cessation of the Panadeine forte and antipsychotic medication.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OUTCOME" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The patient made a complete recovery after 1 week.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Mania can be induced by large doses of Panadeine forte, particularly if there is a biological predisposition.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
